why One-time quests worth 2,000 and big wins make it the quickest of the four; Exalted gives a Legacy Point.

# Stormpike Guard (730, Alliance) and Frostwolf Clan (729, Horde).
# Built from Forever's quest data (quest pages: reputation per quest and the
# objectives), the world database's standing gates (the insignia quests),
# Forever's NPC data (places, on-kill reputation, quartermasters' lists),
# Forever's object data (tower and banner places) and the Forever client's
# item table (prices before any standing discount). Exalted with either
# faction is the Legacy Challenge "Master of Alterac Valley" (one
# account-wide Legacy Point). The mounts have their own guides
# (forever/collectibles/mounts/alliance/stormpike-battle-charger,
# forever/collectibles/mounts/horde/frostwolf-howler).
#
# Forever's quest pages give the repeatable turn-ins inside the battleground
# (More Armor Scraps 6781 / More Booty! 6741, Irondeep and Coldtooth Supplies,
# Crystal Cluster 7386 / A Gallon of Blood 7385, the harnesses and stables)
# only Ironforge or Orgrimmar reputation, no Stormpike or Frostwolf: they are
# left to notes. The Classic body-part bounties and "Wanted" posters (7361-
# 7366, 7401, 7402) and Korrak the Everliving (7382) have no Forever page.
# Reputation for towers, captains and generals inside the battle is the
# Classic figure (12 a tower, graveyard or mine, 125 a captain, about 300 a
# general); Forever has published no battleground reputation rates.
# ASSUMED: 3 Marks of Honor for a win and 1 for a loss (Classic flow;
# Forever's data has no per-match reward). In-game check: marks after a game.
# INGAME: Forever's item table lists no standing on any Alterac Valley reward
# but the draughts (in Classic: the tabard and the Superior Draughts at
# Friendly, the cloaks, pendants, belts and Major Draughts at Honored, the
# weapons and the battle standard at Revered, the rest and the mounts at
# Exalted; the guide names each at that standing). Does the quartermaster
# still ask for it?

step Lieutenant Rotimer
  only Alliance
  zone Ironforge
  tip Alterac Valley is a 40 against 40 battle for level 51 and up, and the fastest of the four battleground reputations: it has about 2,000 reputation of one-time quests, and a full win pays several hundred. The same one-time quests also pay 1,870 Ironforge reputation. Lieutenant Rotimer recruits outside the Great Forge. Forever's Legacy Diplomat perk adds up to 10% to every number in this guide.
  accept 7261                          -- The Sovereign Imperative, 100

step Lieutenant Haggerdin
  only Alliance
  zone Alterac Mountains
  tip The Stormpike camp stands outside the Alterac Valley gate, on the Alterac Mountains side above Hillsbrad. Take every quest here: they all pay 100 or more, once.
  turnin 7261
  accept 7162                          -- Proving Grounds: the Stormpike Banner in Icewing Cavern, 100
  accept 7081                          -- Sergeant Durgen Stormpike: assault a graveyard, 100
  accept 7102                          -- destroy a tower or bunker banner, 100
  accept 7122                          -- capture a mine, 100

step Dun Baldar
  only Alliance
  zone Alterac Valley
  tip Queue at the gate, at any battlemaster or from the battleground screen; you enter at Dun Baldar in the north. Before the gates open, take the quests in the town: they are done during the battle.
  accept 7121                          -- Mountaineer Boombellow: The Quartermaster, 10
  turnin 7121
  accept 7223                          -- Murgot Deepforge: 20 Armor Scraps, 100
  accept 7282                          -- Commander Karl Philips: Brotherly Love, 100
  accept 7301                          -- Commander Duffy: Fallen Sky Lords, 100
  accept 7367                          -- Stormpike Explosives Expert: Defusing the Threat, 100

step Icewing Cavern
  only Alliance
  zone Alterac Valley
  tip Icewing Cavern lies southwest of Dun Baldar. The Stormpike Banner stands at the back of the cave, past the yetis and harpies.
  collect 17849 quest 7162.1           -- Stormpike Banner

step The battle
  only Alliance
  zone Alterac Valley
  tip Most of this happens on the way to Drek'Thar. Loot Armor Scraps from Horde players and guards you kill. Assault the Snowfall Graveyard or any Horde graveyard, burn a Horde tower (click its banner), and take Coldtooth Mine. Commander Louis Philips stands at Tower Point; the Frostwolf Explosives Expert at Frostwolf Village. Fallen Sky Lords asks you to find where the three wing commanders landed. In Classic every tower, graveyard or mine paid 12 reputation, Captain Galvangar 125 and Drek'Thar about 300.
  collect 17422 x20 quest 7223.1       -- Armor Scraps
  kill 13756 quest 7081.1              -- assault a graveyard
  kill 13778 quest 7102.1 @48.2,58.7   -- Iceblood Tower banner
  kill 13796 quest 7122.1 @44.3,67.9   -- Coldtooth Mine
  kill 13154 quest 7282.1              -- Commander Louis Philips
  kill 14029 quest 7301.1              -- Wing Commander Ichman's spot
  kill 14031 quest 7301.2              -- Wing Commander Vipore's spot
  kill 14030 quest 7301.3              -- Wing Commander Slidore's spot
  kill 13597 quest 7367.1              -- Frostwolf Explosives Expert

step Back in Dun Baldar
  only Alliance
  zone Alterac Valley
  turnin 7223
  turnin 7282
  turnin 7301
  turnin 7367

step Back at the gate
  only Alliance
  zone Alterac Mountains
  tip Your first Alterac Valley Marks of Honor go to the Alliance Brigadier General beside Lieutenant Haggerdin: 150 the first time (Remember Alterac Valley!), then 100 for every 3 more. Forever's PvP gear also costs Marks of Honor along with honor: decide what you want before you hand them in. You can carry at most 30 Alterac Valley marks: hand in or spend them before you reach that.
  turnin 7162                          -- Stormpike Insignia Rank 1
  turnin 7081
  turnin 7102
  turnin 7122
  accept 8375
  collect 20560 x3 quest 8375.1 @39.3,82.3  -- Alterac Valley Marks of Honor: play games
  turnin 8375

step Stormpike Guard to Friendly
  only Alliance
  zone Alterac Mountains
  tip Prospector Stonehewer by the gate wants Drek'Thar dead: win a game in which your team kills him. Then he lets you pick a weapon (Hero of the Stormpike).
  accept 7141 optional                 -- The Battle of Alterac, 200
  turnin 7141 optional
  accept 8271 optional
  turnin 8271 optional                 -- Hero of the Stormpike, 10 and a weapon
  rep 730 Friendly

step Rise and Be Recognized
  only Alliance
  zone Alterac Mountains
  tip Friendly lets Lieutenant Haggerdin upgrade your insignia: 100 reputation. Friendly to Honored is 6000 reputation. In Classic a full win paid 300 to 700 with its 3 marks; the Brigadier General keeps taking 3 marks for 100. Inside, Master Ryson's All Seeing Eye (75, from the Winterax caves) repeats every game; Korrak the Bloodrager (200, when he appears in the middle of the valley) goes back to Lieutenant Haggerdin here. Friendly opens the Stormpike Battle Tabard (1g) and the Superior Healing and Mana Draughts (5s) at Thanthaldis Snowgleam beside him.
  accept 7168
  turnin 7168
  buy 19032 npc 13217                  -- Stormpike Battle Tabard, 1g
  talk 15351 optional                  -- Alliance Brigadier General: Remember Alterac Valley! again, 100 for 3 marks
  rep 730 Honored

step Honored Amongst the Guard
  only Alliance
  zone Alterac Mountains
  tip Honored: insignia rank 3, 100 reputation. Honored to Revered is 12000 reputation. Thanthaldis Snowgleam beside Lieutenant Haggerdin sells the Stormpike Soldier's and Sage's Cloaks and Pendants (about 7g each), the Stormpike belts (4g74s to 7g12s) and the Major Healing and Mana Draughts (10s).
  accept 7169
  turnin 7169
  talk 13217 optional                  -- Thanthaldis Snowgleam
  talk 15351 optional                  -- Alliance Brigadier General: 100 for 3 marks
  rep 730 Revered

step Earned Reverence
  only Alliance
  zone Alterac Mountains
  tip Revered: insignia rank 4, 150 reputation. Revered to Exalted is 21000 reputation, half the climb. Revered opens the weapons at Thanthaldis Snowgleam: Electrified Dagger, Crackling Staff and Stormstrike Hammer (31g65s to 39g85s), and the Stormpike Battle Standard (5g). At 51 and up Concerted Efforts (3 marks each from Alterac Valley, Arathi Basin and Warsong Gulch) pays 200 the first time and 150 after, plus reputation for the other two battlegrounds.
  accept 7170
  turnin 7170
  talk 15351 optional                  -- Alliance Brigadier General: Concerted Efforts
  talk 13217 optional                  -- Thanthaldis Snowgleam: Revered rewards
  rep 730 Exalted

step Legendary Heroes
  only Alliance
  zone Alterac Mountains
  tip Exalted gives the Legacy Point "Master of Alterac Valley" and the last two insignia, 400 reputation that no longer counts for anything but the insignia. Thanthaldis Snowgleam sells the Stormpike Battle Charger (200g, level 60; its own guide), Don Julio's Band and Don Rodrigo's Band (75g56s), The Unstoppable Force (156g49s), The Immovable Object (79g53s), The Lobotomizer (125g66s) and the 50g tomes and off-hands.
  accept 7171
  turnin 7171
  accept 7172
  turnin 7172
  talk 13217 optional                  -- Thanthaldis Snowgleam: Exalted rewards

